  "note": "Native dimensional geometry, not a Blender render. Edit the literal values and render. Front heights and lengths encode exact data on shared scales; the fixed pedestal and fixed seesaw weights are decoration. Seesaw tilt expresses which value is larger, not measured torque or a physical model. The stack preserves any remainder against an explicit total. Keep units and sources visible. Use motion:none for a static presentation. Prefer flat charts for dense, signed or very close comparisons."
